{
  "id": "signaled-avoidance",
  "term": "signaled avoidance",
  "definition": "Signaled avoidance is an aversive learning task in which a cue such as a tone signals an upcoming unpleasant event, and the learner acquires a response that prevents it. It refers to learning to act during the warning signal to avoid the aversive outcome.",
